Verse 1:
[Dm]Let your heart be [F]broken
[F]For a world in [Edim]need:
[Dm]Feed the [F]mouths that hunger,
[Am]Soothe the wounds [C]that bleed,
[C]Give the cup of [Bm]water
[Am]And the loaf of [C]bread—
[Dm]Be [Am]the [C]hands of Jesus,
[Am]Serving in His stead.

Verse 2:
[Dm]Here on earth applying principles [F]of [Am]love,
[Dm]Visible [F]expression ' God still rules [Gm]above
[Am]Living illustration of the Living [C]Word
[Am]To the minds of all who've Never seen or heard.

Verse 3:
[Dm]Blest to be a blessing privileged [F]to [Am]care,
[Dm]Challenged by [F]the need apparent everywhere.
[Am]Where mankind is wanting, fill the vacant [C]place.
[Am]Be the means through which the Lord reveals His grace.

Verse 4:
[Dm]Add to your believing deeds that [F]prove it [Am]true,
[Dm]Knowing Christ [F]as Savior, make Him Master, [Gm]too.
[Am]Follow in His footsteps, go where He [C]has trod;
[Am]In the world's great trouble risk yourself for God.

Verse 5:
[Dm]Let your heart be tender and your [F]vision [Am]clear;
[Dm]See mankind [F]as God sees, serve Him far [Gm]and near.
[Am]Let your heart be broken by a brother's [C]pain;
[Am]Share your rich resources, give and give again.
